  "notes": [
   "A depth-three clone of a ten-commit upstream. The three commits that came over were rewritten: the window's first commit has no parent at all, because there is nothing below the cut to point at, and `.git/shallow` names the tip. A history walker that walks to the root instead of to the shallow cut will ask for an object that is not in this repository and fail with a message nobody in the product can act on, so the corpus contains the shape and names the cut."
